[2026-01-30T16:12:19.918Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Implementation: Create animated story mode with auto-narrated timeline playback and exportable video timeline summaries\n\n## Context Area\nTimeline & Flow Visualizations\n\n## Description\nCreate animated story mode with auto-narrated timeline playback and exportable video timeline summaries\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n## Animated Story Mode with Timeline Playback\n\n### Vision\nCreate a story mode that animates through the timeline like a documentary, auto-narrating key events and creating a compelling narrative from research data. Export as video or interactive presentation.\n\n### Business Value\n- Makes research accessible to non-analyst stakeholders\n- Creates shareable content for presentations\n- Documentary-style delivery increases engagement\n- Supports executive briefings\n- Premium feature for storytelling needs\n\n### Scope\n**Included:**\n- Animated timeline playback with smooth transitions\n- Auto-generated narration script from events\n- Pause/play/seek controls\n- Speed adjustment (0.5x - 3x)\n- Chapter markers for key periods\n- Event highlight animations\n- Context cards that appear at events\n- Export as video or animated GIF\n- Interactive presentation mode\n- Background music with event-synced cues\n\n**Out of Scope:**\n- Full video editing (cuts, transitions between scenes)\n- Custom narration recording\n\n### Key Components\n1. **StoryModePlayer** - Main playback container\n2. **TimelineAnimator** - Controls timeline progression\n3. **EventHighlighter** - Animation when event appears\n4. **ContextCard** - Info cards for events\n5. **NarrationGenerator** - AI script from events\n6. **ChapterNavigator** - Jump between key periods\n7. **PlaybackControls** - Play/pause/speed/seek\n8. **StoryExporter** - Export to video/GIF\n9. **MusicSynchronizer** - Background music integration\n\n### Technical Approach\n- RequestAnimationFrame for smooth playback\n- AI (Claude/GPT) for narration script generation\n- Web Speech API or TTS for narration audio\n- RecordRTC for video capture\n- Tone.js for music synchronization\n- Chapter detection via event clustering\n- GSAP or Framer Motion for animations\n\n### Files to Create/Modify\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/story/StoryModePlayer.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/story/TimelineAnimator.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/story/EventHighlighter.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/story/ContextCard.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/story/NarrationGenerator.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/story/ChapterNavigator.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/story/PlaybackControls.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/story/StoryExporter.tsx`\n- Create: `src/lib/storyScript.ts` - Script generation\n- Create: `src/hooks/useStoryPlayback.ts`\n- Modify: Timeline.tsx - Add story mode toggle\n\n### Success Criteria\n- Playback feels smooth and cinematic\n- Narration naturally describes events\n- Context cards provide relevant information\n- Chapters break story into logical segments\n- Export produces watchable video\n- Interactive mode allows exploration during playback\n- Music enhances without distracting\n\n### Potential Challenges\n- Narration timing with variable event density\n- Cinematic pacing for uneven data\n- Video export performance and quality\n- Music licensing for exports\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n5. Test the changes work as expected\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\nFocus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb700aba-f9fc-4283-93cf-561e37220b63","uuid":"bb279750-1165-4087-9439-9a6ad81c6bdc","isSynthetic":true}
